00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.920
I... have to do <i>that</i>?!

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.800
I'm up on top...?

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.800
Hey, take a look at the top screen!

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.630
They're fighting for the top!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.090
Grab me that top cup!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.710
No, don't take a close-up!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:24.840
Don't mix up my cup
of noodles with yours!

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.760
Hop, step, jump!

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:36.590
Ain't that great, Haru?
You're on the top!

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.090
Wanna switch with me, Haru?

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:43.050
Don't. Kazu and Haru have
the best physique for flyers.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:45.420
That might be true, but...

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:48.550
I think being a flyer is...

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.510
Do you have a problem with it?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.550
That's not it...

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.510
Since you're shy, you don't
want to stand out.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:58.210
That's not it, either.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.510
Oh, Mizoguchi!

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.090
I come bearing good news.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.880
Who's that? A pin-up girl?

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.010
A member of Dreams, the Meishiin
Women's Cheerleading Team.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.630
I arranged for us to practice
together in the future.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:18.510
With a joint training session.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:22.260
Female cheerleaders?

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.420
In miniskirts?

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.460
Miniskirts, indeed.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.170
Go, fight, win!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.420
Aren't you confusing this
with a speed-dating session?

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.210
I want to see some stunts up-close.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.550
I don't know much about
the spotter's movements..

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.010
You've got a point.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.260
I want to see how the bases move around.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.880
Mizoguchi, when will this take place?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.380
In two weeks.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:53.960
Good, let's perfect the Elevator and Extension
by then so that we can show it to them!

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:56.840
They actually have a proper coach.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.670
This is a great chance
to get some feedback.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:02.460
Think we can pull it off in two weeks, Sho?

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.920
Sho?

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.050
Yeah! Just barely.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.170
All right! Let's show those
girls what we're made of!

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.590
I'd certainly like to.

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:18.800
You, too? Then I won't back down, either.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:23.380
Haru and Kazu are so lucky.
You flyers are gonna be chick magnets.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.880
S'heavy!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.880
Spotter, hold him steady!

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.710
R-Right!

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.460
Now bend your knees once, and use
the momentum from extending your legs

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.880
to lift him with your whole body!

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:42.590
Flyer, stand up quickly!

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.880
Well, look at that.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.760
It's just like you said, standing up
all at once makes it easier to stay balanced.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.710
Kazu's amazing!

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:50.710
Yeah...

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.380
Now you switch with them.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.800
Huh? All right.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.710
Bend your knees...

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.800
Use the momentum from extendin' your legs...

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.920
And lift... with your whole body!

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.050
Straighten your knees!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.630
Uh, okay.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.880
Keep your body upright!

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.460
Put him down for a minute!

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:18.380
I'm sorry. I couldn't support you properly.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.670
No, that's not the problem, Ton.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.590
I'm the one to blame.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:23.960
I...

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.590
Let's try it again.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:31.880
It'll be fine. You'll get it bit by bit.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.920
I'll be supporting you, so don't worry.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.510
Yeah...

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.550
It's just no use.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:56.550
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:56.720
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.180
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:57.390
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:57.430
Once you get the hang of it,
you'll master this in no time!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:57.430
Kazuma

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:57.550
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:57.470
Once you get the hang of it,
you'll master this in no time!

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:57.470
Kazuma

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:57.510
Once you get the hang of it,
you'll master this in no time!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:57.510
Kazuma

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:57.550
Once you get the hang of it,
you'll master this in no time!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:57.550
Kazuma

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.550
I'm sorry, Kazu. I can't do this.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.550
Once you get the hang of it,
you'll master this in no time!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:58.550
Kazuma

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.630
Kazu...!

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.590
I'm starting something new with you.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.880
Go, fight, win!

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.670
Good, now you've got
the Extension down, too.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.380
Kazu's simply incredible.

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:26.590
Stand! Stand up, Haru!

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:28.800
Oh no!

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.210
Haru!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.170
Are you all right, Haru?

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.420
What's wrong?

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.460
I can't do it.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.840
I've been meaning to tell
you this for ages, but...

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:47.420
I'm afraid of heights.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.880
Wasn't that just when we were kids?
I mean, you go on your roof...

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.170
I still can't look down from there.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:59.300
Since everyone's been trying so hard,
I just couldn't bring myself to say anything...

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:01.010
I'm so sorry.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:05.630
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.460
What a shockin' revelation.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.510
--Get a clue!

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.420
--Ow!
--Get a clue!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.760
Our joint training session
is the day after tomorrow...

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.090
I wonder if we could postpone it?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.960
Wait, we've got Professor Risujiro here!

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:21.840
Oh! You can take Haru's
place just this once.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.010
About that...

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:27.590
I can't go to our joint training session.

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:28.800
Why not?

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.880
This is the first I've heard of it.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:34.010
I... have a part-time job.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:35.670
That's news to me, too.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:39.300
Can't you take a day off?
Where you workin'?

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.840
At the restaurant...
in front of the train station.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.210
Huh? I'm starting work there tomorrow...

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.550
Wha...?

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:51.510
Anyway, I'm out.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.210
I can't go.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.550
What? Not even for miniskirts?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.760
Though I admit that's not the point...

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.010
Come on in.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:14.710
Stop that, you'll scare the customers away.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.800
Look, here's one. Go seat him.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.630
This is a bad sign...

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:20.960
Haru...

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.050
You can't practice cheerleading
with a face like that.

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:33.880
I really am sorry for not
noticing anything was wrong.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.670
I'm sorry, too.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:38.760
For not realizing that your
mother was a cheerleader.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:44.630
I had no idea that you
wanted to do cheerleading.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:54.760
I'll be our flyer tomorrow!

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.630
You just show them your
tumbling and the motions!

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:04.710
These guys...

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.450
Ton

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.450
Haru, you're coming tomorrow, right?

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.450
Gen

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.450
It's worth going just for the miniskirts!

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:13.880
Go, fight, win!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:18.630
5, 6, 7, 8! Go, go, Dreams! We're #1!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.880
I can't hear you!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.050
Right!

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.130
The hell is this?

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:31.010
It's her...

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.550
Amazing.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:36.800
Yeah.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.550
You there, what are you doing?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:47.210
We're the Men's Cheerleading Club, here for
the joint training session as promised.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.210
Joint training session?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:57.090
I'm Takagi, an OG of Dreams.
I now serve as its coach.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.300
I'm Hashimoto of the
Men's Cheerleading Club.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:03.760
There was no such thing as an all men's team
back when I was a cheerleader...

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.920
And your team name?

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:07.340
We don't have one yet.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.550
We only started a month ago.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:13.260
So... you said that since
you're a good team,

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:19.420
we could having a meaningful
joint training session, yes?

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:22.130
Everything begins with a meeting.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:27.210
I guess we have no choice.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:31.260
As promised, we'll watch you practice.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.920
Thank you very much!

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:38.510
Since we're just starting out, we hope
you'll be generous with your advice!

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.760
Go, fight, win!

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:45.510
Bases! Your elbows are
too low! Lift them higher!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.760
Right!

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.920
Spotter, pay attention!

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:51.260
Right!

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.800
Flyer, your posture is terrible!

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.380
Straighten up your arms!

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:55.800
Right!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:58.460
Good enough. Come down for now.

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.340
What are your positions?

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:03.260
I'm a base.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.590
And you?

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:08.590
A flyer... for now.

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:11.090
What do you mean "for now"?

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:13.210
Switch with them and show me.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.130
This is bad!

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.960
Didn't you come here to practice?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.210
No, Haru is...

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.090
I'll do it.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.300
But...

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:24.670
I'll do the Elevator.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.710
Don't look down! Keep your knees straight!

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:31.510
Right!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:33.550
Get your rear in gear!

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:39.420
Let's go, Dreams!

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:45.460
How do you think we achieve
such stability with our stunts?

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.460
You master the basics?

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:53.260
Yes. Basics are one part of it.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:54.710
What else?

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:56.260
Technique?

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.960
Yes, technique is also important.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:03.260
You boys are trying to
brute force this, right?

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:09.010
But with good technique, even a less
muscular girl can do stunts with poise and grace.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.170
One more important thing is trust.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:15.090
You can pull off difficult feats only
if you believe in your teammates.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:21.340
You can jump from a high place when you
know that someone will always catch you.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:23.960
That is what you lack.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:30.210
You can't stand up during the Elevator
because you don't trust your teammates.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.460
I don't trust them...?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.510
Your juice is ready.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:45.710
So we meet again.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.170
You're a member of Dreams, right?

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.670
I'm Chihiro Sakai.

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.260
Nice to meet you...

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.010
See ya.

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.300
Coach Takagi doesn't yell
at unmotivated people.

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.010
Huh?

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.670
Try your best!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.760
Isn't that...?

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.010
Haru's late.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.340
Yeah...

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.710
It's you guys!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.300
Kazu, I just saw--

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.550
Domoto, these were the ones
saying all that stupid stuff.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.340
Stupid stuff?

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.760
Oh? What are you two doing here?

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.960
What's up?

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.920
We have a meeting about next
month's joint demonstration.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:45.170
I see.

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.420
I'll introduce you.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.550
This is Domoto, team captain of Sparks
at Yomei University, and this is Hanasaki.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:54.840
Jin Domoto.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.630
Kaoru Hanasaki.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.840
Uh, nice to meet you.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:02.550
Takagi, what's your
connection to these guys?

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:05.340
They're the Meishiin
Men's Cheerleading Club.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:09.260
Men's Cheerleading?
You're an all-men's team?

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.630
Yes!

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:14.090
I'm pleased to see more
like-minded individuals.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:20.550
But if you're just myopic enough to be seduced
by the glamour of it all, then give up now.

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:24.340
Countless people quit my team every year.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:27.800
Cheerleading isn't a sport for
people who kid themselves.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.800
Domoto's right.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.760
If you want to improve,
then you need a coach.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:37.210
Have you worked with one yet?

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:39.210
Someone who couldn't come today, Sho--

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:42.260
Uh, a gymnast with some experience...

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:45.300
Sho? You mean Sho Tokugawa?

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.960
Do you know him?

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.090
So he didn't quit cheerleading?

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.630
Figures he'd be back.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.550
I wonder what happened between them?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:04.300
Everybody's got things
they don't want to talk about.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.020
Sho

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.020
How was the joint training session?

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:08.130
It's Sho.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:12.670
Why don't we call him and have
a meeting to discuss the day?

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:16.670
But I'm not really in the mood
for Caf Sunflower...

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:20.170
Come over to my place.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.460
Bandou Gym

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.300
So this is the roof you spoke of.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.630
Mizoguchi...

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.630
It's not that high at all!

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.630
Ow!

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:38.800
Well, since it's available,
can't we practice up here, too?

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.630
That's certainly true.

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.760
Let's get this meeting started!

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.800
If there's one thing we regret today...

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.670
...it's that we didn't get to
chat with any of the girls.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.840
Though we did make friends with the OG.

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:51.420
Are you a masochist?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.550
What does OG stand for, anyway?

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:57.800
Old Girl. But more like
One Giant Forehead.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.130
Sho, hey there!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:02.420
So this is the roof you mentioned.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:05.170
We're done talking about that.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:07.670
All right. So...

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:10.420
How was the joint training session?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.920
Those cheerleaders... All of them...

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:18.460
They were practicin'
a million times better than us.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:23.170
They were freakin' amazing,
though it pains me to say so.

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:26.460
We seriously sucked.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:29.010
Completely, utterly sucked.

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.300
I see.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.710
Their coach said I don't trust anyone.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.050
It's my fault.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:38.210
It's not.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:41.880
In cheerleading, one person
can't do everything alone.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.670
The people who jump,
and the people who catch them...

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:47.420
When everyone trusts each other...

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:50.210
...then they finally perfect those stunts.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:53.630
"If you give up when things go wrong,
then a failure stays a failure.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.550
If you persist until you succeed,
then a failure becomes a success."

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:01.550
Dixit Konosuke Matsushita,
founder of Panasonic.

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:05.130
Yes! Let's keep going
until we succeed. Right?

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:06.380
Right!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.460
Yeah!

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:10.670
Sho, we'll be counting on
more of your Spartan training.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:12.300
Fine.

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.090
We also have to think of a team name.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.010
The Megane Seven.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:16.800
You're the only one with glasses!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:17.920
Cherry Boys.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.420
That only applies to you, too!

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.210
Huh?

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.130
I vote for Team Risujiro!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:24.260
Absolutely not.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.090
Y'know, I want to break a few things.

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.710
The assumptions of those who won't
recognize men's cheerleading,

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.460
the expectations of those
who say we can't succeed...

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:37.710
I want to break through Mizoguchi's
sayings to reveal his true self.

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:42.340
I want to break apart
Ton's sense of self-doubt.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.840
Haru's... sense of guilt.

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:51.420
And whatever is weighing down Sho.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.210
I have sumthin' I wanna
break apart, too.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.960
Your babe-less self?

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.840
Look who's talkin'!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:03.050
I want to break it, too.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:07.260
I want to break apart...
my former self.

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:11.090
We'll break it all to smithereens.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:17.090
The beliefs of everyone who says
it's impossible, and our own selves!

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:18.880
Breaking...

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.210
Break...

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:21.760
Breaker...

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.550
Breakers!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.760
We are the Breakers!

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:32.170
That's it!

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:33.960
Cheesy, but it works.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:36.010
It's the next best thing to The Megane Seven.

00:21:36.010 --> 00:21:37.300
Yeah!

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.090
Right, let's do this!

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:52.840
The seven of us will break it all!

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:08.210
Here we go!

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:09.880
Go, fight, win!

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:14.340
Let's go, Breakers!

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:22.050
What We Want To Break

00:22:32.010 --> 00:22:35.590
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:35.590 --> 00:22:42.170
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.590
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:48.960
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:52.260
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:58.840
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:22:58.840 --> 00:23:01.760
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:05.050
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:07.130
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:08.800
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.300
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:16.670
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:20.420
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.050
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.840
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:36.840 --> 00:23:40.210
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:43.550 --> 00:23:48.340
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:53.670 --> 00:23:54.710
Don't look so down.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.340
To think that you're our dark horse.

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:57.840
I guess this is the end of Cherry Boys.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:00.920
If you show how cool you are onstage,
you're sure to pick up a girl or two!

00:24:00.920 --> 00:24:01.920
Two girlfriends?

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:03.050
Maybe.

00:24:03.050 --> 00:24:05.680
Let's break it all to smithereens, guys.

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:10.050
Next Episode: Let's Go, Breakers!

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:09.930
Go! Fight! Win!
